      "data": {
        "text": "All required Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here is a summary of the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] encrypt_payload.py**: Encrypts a plaintext payload using Azure Key Vault.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] decrypt_payload.py**: Decrypts a ciphertext payload using Azure Key Vault.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] envelope_encrypt.py**: Implements envelope encryption using Azure Key Vault.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] sign_or_verify_key.py**: Uses Azure Key Vault for signing or verification.\n5. **[HELPER] security_client.py**: Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Azure Key Vault.\n6. **[HELPER] security_models.py**: Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Azure Key Vault.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] key_usage_summary.py**: Summarizes key usage and crypto events using Azure Key Vault.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] payload_safety.py**: Checks decrypted text payloads for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] crypto_audit_embedding.py**: Embeds crypto audit notes for semantic search.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] compliance_note_translate.py**: Translates encryption or compliance notes for reviewers.\n\nEach scored file uses Azure Key Vault as the concrete external provider, making it identifiable in the code. The local helper files provide configuration and model definitions to support these operations, and the later-step files use the helper files to perform more complex tasks.",
